  "title": "Breaking: Widget Config & ToolCall Ops",
  "summary": "Discovery Engine v1alpha introduces breaking changes: the `autoModelId` field in widget configurations is now read-only, and the `name` parameter for the new `toolCalls.operations.get` method is strictly required. Additionally, a new `get` method for tool call operations and a `taskName` field for conversation feedback are now available.",
  "details": "This update includes two breaking changes. First, the `autoModelId` property within the `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfo` schema is now marked as `readOnly`. If your application attempts to write to this field, it will now result in an error. Second, for the newly introduced `projects.locations.collections.engines.assistants.agents.toolCalls.operations.get` method, the `name` parameter is now strictly required. While the method itself is new, this constraint is flagged as a breaking change.\n\nOn the feature side, developers can now retrieve the status of long-running operations related to agent tool calls using the new `projects.locations.collections.engines.assistants.agents.toolCalls.operations.get` method, enabling polling for operation results. The `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFeedbackConversationInfo` schema also gains an optional `taskName` field, allowing you to link conversation feedback to specific Sobi tasks. Minor modifications include a reordering of OAuth scopes for `completeQuery` methods across various `dataStores` and `engines` resources, swapping `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform` and `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud_search.query`.",
